From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] generator: photon installs ds-identify under libexecdir

The systemd generator template picks the ds-identify path from the build
variant. Photon is absent from the list of variants that use libexecdir, so
it falls through to the else branch and renders

    dsidentify="/usr/lib/cloud-init/ds-identify"

while the meson install puts the binary at

    /usr/libexec/cloud-init/ds-identify

The generator then exits 3, no datasource is ever identified, and all six
cloud-* units stay inactive despite being enabled. Nothing appears in
`systemctl --failed`, so instance configuration - injected SSH keys,
hostname, user-data, network config - is silently not applied.

Photon is an RPM distribution whose meson build installs helpers to
libexecdir, exactly like the variants already listed, so it belongs in that
branch.

Rendering the template confirms the change is scoped to photon:

    before   --variant photon  ->  /usr/lib/cloud-init/ds-identify
    after    --variant photon  ->  /usr/libexec/cloud-init/ds-identify
             --variant rhel    ->  /usr/libexec/cloud-init/ds-identify  (unchanged)
             --variant ubuntu  ->  /usr/lib/cloud-init/ds-identify      (unchanged)

Introduced by the 25.1.3 -> 26.2 upgrade, which moved the install from
%py3_install to %{meson_install} and relocated the payload to libexecdir.
The %files section was updated to match; the generator was not.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
 systemd/cloud-init-generator.tmpl | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/systemd/cloud-init-generator.tmpl b/systemd/cloud-init-generator.tmpl
index 888bad5..312a690 100644
--- a/systemd/cloud-init-generator.tmpl
+++ b/systemd/cloud-init-generator.tmpl
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@ CLOUD_SYSTEM_TARGET="/usr/lib/systemd/system/cloud-init.target"
 CLOUD_SYSTEM_TARGET="/lib/systemd/system/cloud-init.target"
 {% endif %}
 {% if variant in ["almalinux", "azurelinux", "centos", "cloudlinux", "eurolinux", "fedora",
-                  "miraclelinux", "openeuler", "OpenCloudOS", "openmandriva", "rhel", "rocky", "TencentOS", "virtuozzo"] %}
+                  "miraclelinux", "openeuler", "OpenCloudOS", "openmandriva", "photon", "rhel", "rocky", "TencentOS", "virtuozzo"] %}
     dsidentify="/usr/libexec/cloud-init/ds-identify"
 {% elif variant == "benchmark" %}
     dsidentify="/bin/true"
-- 
